{title: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley & Felix Mendelssohn}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}

Verse 1
[F]Hark! the herald [C]angels [F]sing,
"Glory [Bb]to the [C]newborn [F]King;
peace on earth and [C]mercy mild,
[G]God and sinners [C]reconciled!"
[F]Joyful, all ye [Bb]nations rise,
[F]join the triumph [Bb]of the skies;
with the an[Bb]gelic [G]host proclaim,
"[C]Christ is [F]born in [C]Bethle[F]hem!"

Verse 2
[F]Christ, by highest Heav'n [C]adored; [F]Christ
the [Bb]everlasting Lord; Late [C]in [F]time,
behold Him come, Offspring of [C]a virgin's
[G]womb. Veiled in flesh [C]the
[F]Godhead see; Hail th'incarnate [Bb]Deity, Pleased
[F]with us in flesh [Bb]to dwell, Jesus
our Emmanuel. Hark! the [G]herald angels
sing, "Glory [F]to the newborn [C]King!"

Verse 3
[F]Hail the heav'nly Prince of [C]Peace! [F]Hail the
Sun [Bb]of Righteousness! Light [C]and life [F]to
all He brings, Ris'n with healing [C]in His wings.
[G]Mild He lays His [C]glory by,
[F]Born that man no [Bb]more may die.
[F]Born to raise the [Bb]sons of earth, Born to
give them second birth. [G]Hark! the herald
angels sing, "Glory [F]to the newborn [C]King!"

Verse 4
[F]Come, Desire of nations, [C]come, Fix [F]in
us [Bb]Thy humble home; [C]Rise, the [F]woman's
conqu'ring Seed, Bruise in us [C]the serpent's head.
[G]Now display Thy saving [C]power,
[F]Ruined nature now restore; [Bb]Now in
[F]mystic union join Thine [Bb]to ours, and ours
to Thine. Hark! the [G]herald angels
sing, "Glory [F]to the newborn [C]King!"

Verse 5
[F]Adam's likeness, Lord, efface, [C]Stamp Thine [F]image
in [Bb]its place: Second [C]Adam from [F]above,
Reinstate us in Thy love. [C]Let us
[G]Thee, though lost, regain, [C]Thee,
[F]the Life, the inner [Bb]man: O,
[F]to all Thyself impart, [Bb]Formed in each
believing heart. Hark! the [G]herald angels
sing, "Glory [F]to the newborn [C]King!"
